From: DeckReader
Subject: [PATCH] Keep variation selectors invisible when a font lacks them

With HarfBuzz shaping, the last font of the fallback chain passes every
character through filterChar(), which replaced the ones the font has no
glyph for with def_char ('?'). Variation selectors (U+FE00..U+FE0F,
U+E0100..U+E01EF) have no glyph in most text fonts, so "↩︎" (U+21A9
U+FE0E), the back-link of every Standard Ebooks note, was drawn "↩?".
Pass them to HarfBuzz unchanged: it applies and then hides them.
---
diff --git a/crengine/src/lvfont/lvfreetypeface.cpp b/crengine/src/lvfont/lvfreetypeface.cpp
--- a/crengine/src/lvfont/lvfreetypeface.cpp
+++ b/crengine/src/lvfont/lvfreetypeface.cpp
@@ -1047,6 +1047,12 @@
     lChar32 res = getReplacementChar(code);
     if (res != 0)
         return res;
+    // Variation selectors are invisible: HarfBuzz uses them to pick a glyph
+    // variant, then hides them. Replacing them with def_char drew a '?'
+    // after the character they qualify, as in "↩︎" (U+21A9 U+FE0E), the
+    // back-link of every Standard Ebooks note.
+    if ((code >= 0xFE00 && code <= 0xFE0F) || (code >= 0xE0100 && code <= 0xE01EF))
+        return code;
     if (def_char != 0)
         return def_char;
     // If nothing found, let code be
